Chapter: XhciSpeedPsi
  cites Works chapter GopXhci
  cites Works chapter GopUsb

 xHCI 1.2c Table 7-13 is the DEFAULT speed id mapping and footnote 120
 states the condition on it: "The Default Speed ID Values shall be
 presented in PORTSC Port Speed field only if no PSI Dwords are defined
 (PSIC = '0')." Table 7-8 says it from the other side, that a non-zero
 PSIC means "no implied Speed ID mappings apply".

 No emulator can express that. codex-vm reports the defaults, so a
 controller that declares its own Protocol Speed IDs has never been in
 front of this driver and cannot be, which is why the assumption
 survived: every arm agreed with every other arm about what a PORTSC
 speed of 1 means. The capability structure here is built by hand, so
 the arms that fire are the ones the hardware would have to provide.

 The encode arms go the other way, and they exist because Table 6-4
 bits 23:20 defines the Slot Context Speed field's valid values by
 reference to the PORTSC Port Speed field, which Table 5-27 defines as
 the Protocol Speed ID. That field therefore speaks the controller's
 vocabulary: a full-speed device is written as the PSIV the controller
 declared for 12 Mb/s, not as the class. A device behind a hub takes
 its speed from the hub's port status, which carries no PSI value, so
 the encode is a reverse lookup by rate rather than a pass-through.
 `enc absent` asks for SuperSpeed, which these PSI dwords do not
 declare, and must fall back to the class rather than answer zero:
 zero is Undefined Speed and would have the Address Device refused.

 The control arms are the ones that must NOT move. With no extended
 capability pointer, with a capability that does not cover the port,
 and with a capability declaring PSIC zero, the value must come back
 UNCHANGED in both directions. That is the case footnote 120 permits
 and it is every run this tree has ever made, so a change that got it
 wrong would re-point every existing green.

Section: Fixtures

 Each check takes the buffer as a parameter. A nullary def is
 re-evaluated at every mention, so a zero-argument buffer would hand
 each check a fresh zeroed allocation and every arm would read its own
 zeros.

 Layout: an extended capability chain starting at dword offset 2. The
 first link is capability id 1 (Legacy Support), whose next pointer of
 2 dwords carries the walk to the Supported Protocol capability at
 dword offset 4. Hopping a foreign capability to reach the right one is
 part of what is under test.

 Within the Supported Protocol capability (Table 7-8): dword two holds
 Compatible Port Offset in bits 7:0, Compatible Port Count in 15:8 and
 PSIC in 31:28. The PSI dwords follow dword three (Table 7-10): PSIV in
 3:0, PSIE in 5:4, PSIM in 31:16.

  psi-word : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  psi-word (psiv) (psie) (psim) =
    bit-or psiv (bit-or (bit-shl psie 4) (bit-shl psim 16))

  build-psi : Integer -> Integer
  build-psi (buf) =
    let c0 = poke-32 buf 8 (bit-or 1 (bit-shl 2 8))
    in let c1 = poke-32 buf 16 2
    in let c2 = poke-32 buf 24 (bit-or 1 (bit-or (bit-shl 4 8) (bit-shl 3 28)))
    in let p0 = poke-32 buf 32 (psi-word 7 2 12)
    in let p1 = poke-32 buf 36 (psi-word 8 2 480)
    in let p2 = poke-32 buf 40 (psi-word 9 1 1500)
    in 0

  build-nopsi : Integer -> Integer
  build-nopsi (buf) =
    let c0 = poke-32 buf 8 (bit-or 1 (bit-shl 2 8))
    in let c1 = poke-32 buf 16 2
    in let c2 = poke-32 buf 24 (bit-or 1 (bit-shl 4 8))
    in 0

  think-buf : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  think-buf (buf) (b) =
    let w = poke-byte buf 3 b
    in hub-think-time buf

Section: Main

  row : Text, Integer -> Text
  row (name) (v) = name & show v

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let buf = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let b = build-psi buf
    in print-line-uni (row "psi full    : " (xhci-speed-resolve buf 2 0 7))
    let buf2 = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let b2 = build-psi buf2
    in print-line-uni (row "psi high    : " (xhci-speed-resolve buf2 2 0 8))
    let buf3 = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let b3 = build-psi buf3
    in print-line-uni (row "psi low     : " (xhci-speed-resolve buf3 2 0 9))
    let buf4 = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let b4 = build-psi buf4
    in print-line-uni (row "psi undef   : " (xhci-speed-resolve buf4 2 0 5))
    let buf5 = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let b5 = build-psi buf5
    in print-line-uni (row "off port    : " (xhci-speed-resolve buf5 2 9 6))
    let buf6 = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let b6 = build-nopsi buf6
    in print-line-uni (row "psic zero   : " (xhci-speed-resolve buf6 2 0 6))
    print-line-uni (row "no xecp     : " (xhci-speed-resolve 0 0 0 6))
    let bufe = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let be = build-psi bufe
    in print-line-uni (row "enc full    : " (xhci-speed-encode bufe 2 0 1))
    let bufe2 = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let be2 = build-psi bufe2
    in print-line-uni (row "enc high    : " (xhci-speed-encode bufe2 2 0 3))
    let bufe3 = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let be3 = build-psi bufe3
    in print-line-uni (row "enc low     : " (xhci-speed-encode bufe3 2 0 2))
    let bufe4 = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let be4 = build-psi bufe4
    in print-line-uni (row "enc absent  : " (xhci-speed-encode bufe4 2 0 4))
    let bufe5 = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let be5 = build-nopsi bufe5
    in print-line-uni (row "enc psic0   : " (xhci-speed-encode bufe5 2 0 1))
    print-line-uni (row "enc no xecp : " (xhci-speed-encode 0 0 0 1))
    let tb = alloc-zeroed 64 64
    in print-line-uni (row "ttt 0x00    : " (think-buf tb 0))
    let tb1 = alloc-zeroed 64 64
    in print-line-uni (row "ttt 0x20    : " (think-buf tb1 32))
    let tb2 = alloc-zeroed 64 64
    in print-line-uni (row "ttt 0x40    : " (think-buf tb2 64))
    let tb3 = alloc-zeroed 64 64
    in print-line-uni (row "ttt 0x60    : " (think-buf tb3 96))
  end
